uttered:
Affording no secrecy to her knees;
She constantly uttered what was not true;
She flirted and petted, or what have you;

utterance:
So shook me? That, I know not. There were words
That broke in utterance ... melted, in the fire;
Embrace, that was convulsion, ... then a kiss ...

My heart shall tremble not its fate to meet,
My mouth give utterance to any moan.
The yawning oven spits forth fiery spears;
